# Pin LF in the working tree, not just in the object store.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true at the system level, so every
# checkout here was being rewritten to CRLF even though all blobs are stored
# LF-only. Git Bash's patched bash tolerates CRLF while parsing a script, so
# this was mostly benign -- but CRs survive inside heredocs and in any data
# bash reads into a variable, which is a live hazard for the .sh engine and the
# .jsonl fixtures the offline suite feeds through `read`.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf per-repo, so the worktree is identical here and
# on the Linux clones that also refresh these docs.
#
# NOTE: this is not the cause of the -prs/-strict/-repositories test failures on
# Windows. Those come from native jq.exe emitting CRLF, so `while IFS= read -r`
# over jq output keeps a trailing \r. See the Windows gotchas in CLAUDE.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the types that break outright when they carry CRs.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
